5. Format specifications control appearance
Place a colon after the expression to add a format specification:
distance = 12.34567
print(f"Distance: {distance:.2f} km")
.2f means fixed-point notation with two digits after the decimal point. The f-string result is text; distance remains the original float.

Add grouping separators
visitors = 1250000
budget = 9876543.21

print(f"Visitors: {visitors:,}")
print(f"Budget: {budget:,.2f}")
The comma improves an English-style numeric display. Localization rules vary; later applications may use a locale-aware presentation library.


Display percentages
completion = 0.875
print(f"Complete: {completion:.1%}")
Percentage formatting multiplies by 100 for display and adds %, producing 87.5%. The stored value remains 0.875.


Align fields into columns
label = "Temperature"
value = 21.5

print(f"{label:&lt;16} | {value:&gt;8.2f}")
print(f"{'Humidity':&lt;16} | {0.62:&gt;8.1%}")

&lt;16 left-aligns text in a field 16 characters wide;
&gt;8.2f right-aligns a two-decimal number in a field eight characters wide.

Fill and center a heading:
print(f"{' NIGHT REPORT ':=^32}")
= is the fill character, ^ centers, and 32 is the field width.


Display signs explicitly
change = 4.2
loss = -1.7

print(f"Change: {change:+.1f}")
print(f"Change: {loss:+.1f}")
+ in the specification displays a sign for both positive and negative values.


